---
import Article from "../components/article.astro";
import Heading from "../components/heading.astro";
import { SetConlangName } from "../components/morphology/set-conlang-name";
import Paragraph from "../components/paragraph.astro";
import { Popup } from "../components/popup";
import SectionLayout from "../layouts/section.astro";
---

<SectionLayout title="Morphology" nextPath="/morphemes">
  <Article>
    <Heading>Hello!</Heading>

    <Paragraph>Welcome to <i>remorphable.</i></Paragraph>

    <Paragraph>
      Through this interactive web experience, you will get an introduction to
      <b>morphology</b>, one of the many fascinating branches of
      <Popup client:load triggerText="linguistics">
        <span>
          Linguistics is the scientific study of language, including learning
          how it is structured, developed, and used.
        </span>
        <span>
          It does <b>not</b> mean learning a specific language or languages (a common
          misconception), although linguists <i>may</i> end up learning languages
          that they are analyzing.
        </span>
      </Popup>. You will learn about some of the basic concepts in morphology,
      including morphemes, lexemes, allomorphy, inflection, derivation, and
      more. These words may sound intimidating at the moment, but fret not! Very
      soon you’ll have a good understanding of what each of these concepts mean
      and why they’re important.
    </Paragraph>

    <Paragraph>
      The fun part? <b>You’ll get to build your own language!</b> Incorporating what
      you learn at each stage, you’ll gradually give shape to a conlang that gets
      more morphologically rich as you progress through the website.
    </Paragraph>

    <SetConlangName client:idle />
  </Article>
</SectionLayout>
